        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0301" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg229"/>

                <head>No. 121.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 21, 1882</date>.
                        (Received May 3.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 346.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acquaint you that
                    immediately after receiving your No. 333 of the 17th of March, in relation to
                    the case of Mr. James L. White, I addressed a letter to Lord Granville upon the
                    subject, and I have just now received his answer, informing me of the discharge
                    of Mr. White. I inclose a copy of this correspondence.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. B. LOWELL.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d121-a1.xml" xpointer="d121-a1"/>
